WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.796
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:02.066 --> 00:03.067
[dramatic synth music playing]

3
00:06.111 --> 00:08.239
[gentle whimsical music playing]

4
00:16.163 --> 00:19.542
[whimsical orchestral music playing]

5
00:26.590 --> 00:27.925
[magical shimmering]

6
00:30.094 --> 00:33.097
-[orchestral music continues] -[goblet thudding]

7
00:35.516 --> 00:36.725
[cat meowing]

8
00:47.987 --> 00:51.532
-[paper tearing] -[handcuffs clanking]

9
00:55.286 --> 01:00.124
-[gentle piano music playing] -[water trickling]

10
01:02.918 --> 01:04.837
[Yi-jun] A day with Managing Director Yoon.

11
01:06.839 --> 01:08.299
Hey, I'm Yoon Yi-jun.

12
01:09.258 --> 01:10.843
Sure, I already know what you're thinking.

13
01:11.552 --> 01:13.470
The beverage of choice for a chaebol

14
01:13.554 --> 01:16.849
is probably organic tea at a certain temperature,

15
01:16.932 --> 01:20.269
and they have their secretary make it precisely to order.

16
01:20.352 --> 01:21.979
[chuckles]

17
01:22.062 --> 01:24.565
Well, that's not what I'm into. Here's what I like.

18
01:24.815 --> 01:26.567
I start things off with a cup of coffee,

19
01:27.651 --> 01:28.694
and I brewed it myself.

20
01:31.280 --> 01:32.364
Mm.

21
01:38.245 --> 01:39.872
[director] Cut.

22
01:39.955 --> 01:41.707
Thanks, everyone. Great work.

23
01:42.041 --> 01:44.001
That was great, sir. The lines were perfect.

24
01:44.084 --> 01:45.127
-Here you go. -[Si-hyun] Oh.

25
01:45.210 --> 01:46.462
-[Da-woon] How was that? -Oh… Wait.

26
01:46.545 --> 01:48.589
Tastes like burnt bean water.

27
01:48.672 --> 01:50.674
You want me to keel over and die right here?

28
01:50.758 --> 01:53.218
I tried to stop this, sir. They insisted, though.

29
01:53.302 --> 01:55.387
70% of our employees drink coffee, so

30
01:55.471 --> 01:57.306
to make it more relatable, we had to do this.

31
01:57.431 --> 01:59.099
-Bring me water. -[Da-woon] Water.

32
01:59.183 --> 02:01.602
-Buddy, the wink's great. -It's your dumb idea.

33
02:01.685 --> 02:04.355
Oh, right. Another thing, I forgot to teach you this one.

34
02:04.438 --> 02:06.273
Go. Get him out.

35
02:06.357 --> 02:09.526
[laughs] Wow. Yeah.

36
02:10.861 --> 02:13.072
The proposal you sent over looks pretty good.

37
02:13.447 --> 02:14.740
Yep, definitely awesome.

38
02:14.823 --> 02:17.785
That goes without saying. Oh, can you hold on a second, please?

39
02:19.370 --> 02:22.581
Leaders should be great communicators. Super essential.

40
02:23.832 --> 02:25.334
-[camera shutter clicks] -[Yi-jun] Cut.

41
02:25.417 --> 02:26.794
[rowing machine whirs]

42
02:30.464 --> 02:35.052
I'm a fan of all sports: rowing, basketball, baseball, so--

43
02:36.178 --> 02:37.262
[cheeky music playing]

44
02:37.346 --> 02:38.472
Soc…

45
02:41.016 --> 02:43.060
Soccer, tennis. I like doing them all.

46
02:43.394 --> 02:46.689
I've always felt sports are great for encouraging teamwork.

47
02:49.733 --> 02:53.487
Though there isn't much to reveal, I'd like to show you all the real Yi-jun.

48
02:53.570 --> 02:55.197
So take a look. More coming up.

49
02:56.281 --> 02:57.408
[sighs]

50
02:57.491 --> 02:58.951
My apologies, sir.

51
02:59.994 --> 03:02.329
Do you know why I take Gongjin Dan's deer antler velvet

52
03:02.413 --> 03:04.415
and wild ginseng during seasonal changes?

53
03:04.498 --> 03:06.792
Because I want to stay healthy without working out.

54
03:06.875 --> 03:07.918
I know. I'm sorry.

55
03:08.585 --> 03:10.462
Get the name of whoever's terrible idea this was.

56
03:11.463 --> 03:12.923
I want name, rank, everything.

57
03:14.341 --> 03:16.010
Because of the Miss Han thing,

58
03:16.343 --> 03:18.429
your name's brought up around the office a lot.

59
03:18.971 --> 03:21.890
The higher-ups aren't happy with you. The interview is all that's left.

60
03:22.016 --> 03:23.308
Please, it's just 30 minutes.

61
03:23.851 --> 03:25.519
That's right.

62
03:25.602 --> 03:28.355
They're just worried about me staining the Taekang legacy.

63
03:28.439 --> 03:29.523
[somber music playing]

64
03:29.732 --> 03:32.151
I'd forgotten I had that.

65
03:32.943 --> 03:34.486
-[gentle piano music playing] -I don't know.

66
03:34.862 --> 03:36.280
You're, uh… you're talking about lying?

67
03:36.363 --> 03:37.364
[laughs]

68
03:37.448 --> 03:38.741
I don't do that at all.

69
03:38.824 --> 03:40.159
Plus, I'm terrible at it.

70
03:42.327 --> 03:45.873
Speaking of which, Taekang has an unblemished reputation,

71
03:45.956 --> 03:49.585
and this legacy continues. Absolutely honest as we've always been.

72
03:50.002 --> 03:51.170
[Jae-hee] What a load of BS.

73
03:51.962 --> 03:53.547
Wow. [sighs]

74
03:53.797 --> 03:56.341
I guess denying everything was him being honest, huh?

75
03:56.425 --> 03:57.968
He's a great actor. I'll give him that.

76
03:58.635 --> 04:02.890
Oh, Yoon Yi-jun's a maestro. We know this. Question is, can you get on his level?

77
04:03.182 --> 04:04.850
You're undercover starting tomorrow.

78
04:05.517 --> 04:06.977
[Wan-gu] Detective Kang's quick on her feet.

79
04:07.061 --> 04:09.521
So long as she keeps her cool, she'll have him tricked.

80
04:09.605 --> 04:11.190
And therein lies the issue. She's way too hotheaded.

81
04:11.273 --> 04:13.025
-What are you talking about, Captain? -Hey, easy.

82
04:13.108 --> 04:15.277
-Ah, you see that right there. -Okay, listen.

83
04:15.360 --> 04:19.323
When you're undercover, try and stay relaxed and keep composure.

84
04:19.406 --> 04:21.533
That's what I do. You can't go in like…

85
04:21.617 --> 04:24.578
[imitating monkey]

86
04:25.662 --> 04:27.206
That's basically the gist of it.

87
04:27.956 --> 04:28.832
Can I kill you?

88
04:29.583 --> 04:30.918
-[laughs] -Let's just trust her.

89
04:31.585 --> 04:33.212
[tense dramatic music playing]

90
04:33.378 --> 04:34.838
Just you wait, Captain.

91
04:34.922 --> 04:38.884
I can't wait for the day that I stick that bastard in a cell

92
04:39.843 --> 04:42.221
and see the look on his face when I reveal everything.

93
04:42.971 --> 04:45.474
I will not blow my cover before that day.

94
04:48.352 --> 04:49.937
[eagle screeches]

95
04:53.190 --> 04:54.191
-[popping] -[upbeat music playing]

96
04:54.399 --> 04:55.901
[Kang Min-ji] Starting today, I'll be your personal secretary--

97
04:55.984 --> 04:57.528
Kang Min-ji reporting.

98
04:57.611 --> 04:59.321
[Captain Park] Why should I be the one cleaning?

99
04:59.404 --> 05:00.906
[Seok-jin] I can't help it, I'm doing this.

100
05:01.573 --> 05:02.741
[Captain Park] Look, it's not like I'm some rookie.

101
05:03.367 --> 05:06.036
The lady in there was watching. I had to actually clean.

102
05:06.286 --> 05:08.205
[Yi-jun] I'm afraid this won't do at all, soldier.

103
05:08.288 --> 05:09.915
-Huh? -[Captain Park] Damn it.

104
05:09.998 --> 05:12.876
Huh? What the heck? What's going on?

105
05:12.960 --> 05:14.211
[Yi-jun] It seems that…

106
05:15.003 --> 05:17.673
-I mean, I wasn't sure. -[rhythmic tense music playing]

107
05:17.756 --> 05:18.757
[Jae-hee] No way.

108
05:19.133 --> 05:20.884
Is my cover blown?

109
05:29.476 --> 05:30.519
What?

110
05:32.688 --> 05:34.106
[shimmering whoosh]

111
05:39.027 --> 05:40.279
You've been caught red-handed.

112
05:40.988 --> 05:42.531
[tense dramatic music playing]

113
05:42.614 --> 05:46.493
[Captain Park] Whoa. Uh, is he onto us, huh?

114
05:46.577 --> 05:49.037
-I think he just took the spy cam glasses. -Huh?

115
05:49.121 --> 05:50.122
You think he knows?

116
05:50.455 --> 05:51.582
[grunts]

117
05:52.666 --> 05:53.917
[gulps]

118
05:54.001 --> 05:56.211
[Jae-hee] If it comes to this, there's only one way out.

119
05:56.295 --> 05:57.588
[heartbeat pounding]

120
05:57.796 --> 06:00.382
As I might have expected from a Special Forces veteran.

121
06:02.259 --> 06:05.095
-You're assaulting my eyes. -[shimmering sound effect]

122
06:08.140 --> 06:10.392
Your whole look is a disaster.

123
06:11.018 --> 06:12.311
What do you mean, sir?

124
06:12.853 --> 06:15.606
You understand that I'm the face of Taekang.

125
06:15.689 --> 06:17.065
How do you think it would look

126
06:17.149 --> 06:20.402
if my personal secretary were seen wearing these?

127
06:21.236 --> 06:24.740
I ran out of contact lenses. Those were all I had. Won't happen again.

128
06:24.823 --> 06:25.782
[comical musical sting]

129
06:26.617 --> 06:29.745
[cheeky music playing]

130
06:36.752 --> 06:40.214
Tell me, were you always misunderstood?

131
06:41.340 --> 06:44.009
In the military, did anybody ask you on a date?

132
06:47.012 --> 06:49.389
No one's ever told you that you're beautiful?

133
06:50.766 --> 06:51.975
You're the beautiful one, sir.

134
06:53.143 --> 06:54.311
You've got nice features.

135
06:54.895 --> 06:56.939
By your response, I'd say you've heard it before.

136
06:59.608 --> 07:01.860
Look over there. How many flowers do you see?

137
07:09.576 --> 07:12.496
-I can't quite tell. -I guess your eyesight's not very good.

138
07:15.123 --> 07:16.875
No, wait. Uh…

139
07:18.377 --> 07:19.378
But these…

140
07:19.711 --> 07:21.546
[tense electronic music playing]

141
07:21.755 --> 07:23.173
aren't prescription.

142
07:26.802 --> 07:30.973
You really thought that I'd never figure it out, huh? [scoffs]

143
07:31.056 --> 07:33.517
-[glasses cracking] -[static crackling]

144
07:33.600 --> 07:35.936
[Captain Park] Whoa. What's happening? What's wrong with it?

145
07:36.645 --> 07:39.022
-We lost connection? -It's not on our end, though.

146
07:39.690 --> 07:41.149
We got a murder suspect chaebol here.

147
07:41.984 --> 07:42.901
You locked and loaded?

148
07:42.985 --> 07:45.153
-Where's the stab vest? -Back there, sir.

149
07:47.447 --> 07:48.740
We're dealing with a lunatic.

150
07:48.824 --> 07:49.658
[grunts] Help me put this on.

151
07:50.659 --> 07:52.869
When a lunatic, chaebol or not, gets pissed off,

152
07:53.704 --> 07:54.871
there's always gonna be bloodshed.

153
07:55.789 --> 07:56.873
Wait, who are you talking about?

154
07:56.957 --> 07:58.375
Who else? Gong Jae Yi.

155
07:59.126 --> 08:00.627
[Jae-hee] Ugh, what do I do?

156
08:00.711 --> 08:03.213
[tense dramatic music playing]

157
08:07.092 --> 08:08.677
You're right. I have a secret.

158
08:09.886 --> 08:12.055
It's 'cause I'm sick of people saying I look like a girl.

159
08:12.931 --> 08:15.767
I wore fake glasses so I wouldn't have to hear it on my first day of work.

160
08:17.352 --> 08:18.437
[sighs]

161
08:19.187 --> 08:20.355
I'm sorry, sir.

162
08:21.857 --> 08:23.483
You won't get a second chance.

163
08:24.318 --> 08:25.861
No more secrets.

164
08:27.321 --> 08:29.906
-Keep that in mind. -[pensive music playing]

165
08:29.990 --> 08:30.991
Follow me.

166
08:33.118 --> 08:35.370
[sighs in relief]

167
08:36.496 --> 08:40.208
Oh. Whoa. Gosh.

168
08:40.292 --> 08:42.294
He's totally insane, this guy.

169
08:48.717 --> 08:50.969
[tense music playing]

170
08:52.763 --> 08:54.306
[Jae-hee] Wow.

171
08:54.389 --> 08:55.682
Oh.

172
08:57.934 --> 08:59.353
-[gasps] -[tense music playing]

173
08:59.936 --> 09:02.439
[grunts]

174
09:06.109 --> 09:07.194
Your reflexes are pretty good.

175
09:07.611 --> 09:08.862
[upbeat music playing]

176
09:09.029 --> 09:10.447
Don't ever let your guard down.

177
09:11.740 --> 09:14.326
You're gonna learn what a dangerous world this is.

178
09:14.785 --> 09:15.994
I'm sure you know already.

179
09:20.082 --> 09:22.167
[Jae-hee] He's even crazier than I thought he was.

180
09:22.250 --> 09:23.085
[sighs]

181
09:39.226 --> 09:40.435
[Jae-hee] Chandelier,

182
09:42.312 --> 09:43.313
garden,

183
09:44.731 --> 09:45.941
living room,

184
09:48.068 --> 09:49.069
dining room.

185
09:52.614 --> 09:53.448
On the second floor,

186
09:54.866 --> 09:57.327
there's one, two, three rooms,

187
09:58.203 --> 09:59.538
and a hallway over there.

188
10:00.080 --> 10:01.498
Okay.

189
10:01.581 --> 10:03.125
[soft mysterious music playing]

190
10:08.213 --> 10:10.757
Excuse me, sir, could I use the washroom for a second?

191
10:10.841 --> 10:12.300
You want permission for everything?

192
10:13.635 --> 10:17.139
To eat, to drink water, to breathe too, I imagine.

193
10:17.222 --> 10:18.723
Even to write in your diary?

194
10:19.558 --> 10:20.725
Don't ask me about every little thing.

195
10:21.643 --> 10:22.811
Got it.

196
10:23.687 --> 10:25.439
-[Jae-hee] Could this be her? -[glass clinks]

197
10:25.522 --> 10:27.274
Choi Myung-suk, the housekeeper.

198
10:28.066 --> 10:29.192
Washroom's over there.

199
10:29.276 --> 10:30.360
Oh.

200
10:36.575 --> 10:38.326
You're the new personal secretary?

201
10:38.410 --> 10:40.579
-Yes, that's right. -I'm Choi Myung-suk.

202
10:40.662 --> 10:42.122
I'm in charge of household affairs.

203
10:43.123 --> 10:44.958
But you can call me Myung-suk, though.

204
10:45.167 --> 10:47.419
It's nice to meet you. My name's Kang Jae-hee.

205
10:50.005 --> 10:51.548
You were hired for your looks, I bet.

206
10:53.133 --> 10:57.345
[laughs] You and Mr. Yoon will light up every room you walk into.

207
10:57.429 --> 10:58.722
[laughs]

208
11:05.896 --> 11:08.899
[tense music playing]

209
11:13.528 --> 11:15.989
[Jae-hee] I'm gonna have to constantly stay on my toes.

210
11:16.072 --> 11:18.074
First step, scan the whole place.

211
11:23.163 --> 11:24.623
[gasps]

212
11:26.374 --> 11:27.751
Oh, God.

213
11:27.834 --> 11:29.586
[phone ringing]

214
11:30.003 --> 11:31.004
You all right?

215
11:31.087 --> 11:32.631
-What's going on? -It's okay. I'm fine.

216
11:32.923 --> 11:34.007
It's just…

217
11:34.090 --> 11:36.009
the camera doesn't seem to be working.

218
11:37.677 --> 11:38.845
[Seok-jin] I'm checking on it.

219
11:38.929 --> 11:41.014
We're only picking up audio when the Wi-Fi is good.

220
11:41.097 --> 11:43.391
Without a recharge, we'll lose battery in eight hours.

221
11:44.267 --> 11:45.977
Where's the captain? Is he there with you?

222
11:46.311 --> 11:47.896
[Jae-hee] I'm worried this camera won't help us.

223
11:48.104 --> 11:49.981
Yeah, okay. What other choice is there?

224
11:50.106 --> 11:51.233
What, you got a better idea?

225
11:51.775 --> 11:54.819
Yoon Yi-jun. It seems like he doesn't trust anybody.

226
11:54.903 --> 11:56.404
I'll start by winning him over.

227
11:56.488 --> 11:57.656
What?

228
11:57.739 --> 11:58.907
You wanna get close?

229
11:58.990 --> 12:01.952
I'll be able to strike once his barriers are lowered.

230
12:02.494 --> 12:04.162
I'll convince him to let his guard down.

231
12:05.288 --> 12:06.206
Can you do that?

232
12:07.207 --> 12:09.334
Let my actions speak. You'll see for yourself.

233
12:09.709 --> 12:12.003
I'll handle this on my own. You're free to fall back.

234
12:12.128 --> 12:13.129
Salute.

235
12:13.505 --> 12:14.589
Salute.

236
12:22.180 --> 12:23.390
[cat hisses]

237
12:23.473 --> 12:24.641
[dramatic sting]

238
12:25.392 --> 12:28.186
-[dramatic whoosh] -[cat screeches]

239
12:28.270 --> 12:29.271
[gasps]

240
12:31.690 --> 12:34.317
[tense dramatic music playing]

241
12:34.401 --> 12:35.694
-[grunts] -[body thuds]

242
12:36.403 --> 12:39.322
[gasps] Are you okay? Oh, no.

243
12:39.406 --> 12:40.532
Mr. Yoon, are you all right?

244
12:40.907 --> 12:43.243
I'm so sorry, sir. That cat appeared out of nowhere.

245
12:43.827 --> 12:45.829
I didn't see you. I'm so sorry.

246
12:45.912 --> 12:48.748
[gasps] There's some… uh…

247
12:48.832 --> 12:50.041
[gasps]

248
12:50.125 --> 12:51.710
[Myeong-sook] Mr. Kim, I'm changing the litter now.

249
12:51.793 --> 12:53.503
Oh my gosh! Oh no.

250
12:54.504 --> 12:56.339
Oh, Mr. Park.

251
12:56.923 --> 12:59.426
-[screams] -[cries]

252
13:02.387 --> 13:03.972
-[groans] -[yelps]

253
13:05.473 --> 13:09.102
-[screams] -[screams]

254
13:09.269 --> 13:11.688
LOVE IN DISGUISE

255
13:13.148 --> 13:14.524
[cat meows]

256
13:14.816 --> 13:16.318
[growls]

257
13:16.901 --> 13:18.236
You bastard.

258
13:19.529 --> 13:21.323
-[cat meows] -What do you want?

259
13:22.324 --> 13:25.285
[whimsical music playing]

260
13:34.127 --> 13:35.462
[cat meows]

261
13:36.129 --> 13:39.174
Oh, what's wrong, baby? You're waiting for daddy, aren't you?

262
13:39.257 --> 13:40.383
Here, Jerry.

263
13:41.426 --> 13:44.471
[Jae-hee] So he distrusts people, but he's obsessed with this cat?

264
13:45.930 --> 13:48.516
I know. You hate his guts, don't you?

265
13:49.476 --> 13:50.477
What's that?

266
13:50.977 --> 13:54.564
You wanna avenge daddy, huh? No, it's fine, baby. Don't worry.

267
13:55.023 --> 13:59.235
Daddy'll get back at that jerk and make sure he rues the day.

268
13:59.319 --> 14:00.528
-[sighs] -[whimsical music continues]

269
14:09.996 --> 14:12.207
Since Jerry's partly responsible for what happened,

270
14:12.290 --> 14:13.708
I'm willing to let it go.

271
14:13.792 --> 14:15.585
However, if this happens again, you can be sure--

272
14:15.669 --> 14:16.795
It won't happen again.

273
14:18.129 --> 14:19.214
Just so you understand,

274
14:20.131 --> 14:23.343
-I am not a patient person at all. -[tense music playing]

275
14:25.595 --> 14:26.763
They filled you in?

276
14:27.430 --> 14:28.723
Mr. Jung told me everything.

277
14:29.140 --> 14:30.141
What do I dislike?

278
14:30.767 --> 14:32.310
Everything, except for the things you like.

279
14:32.394 --> 14:34.688
-And what are those exactly? -Nothing, sir.

280
14:34.771 --> 14:36.481
[toy squeaks]

281
14:36.690 --> 14:38.233
Correct.

282
14:38.483 --> 14:42.362
Let me rephrase the question. What do I detest more than anything else?

283
14:42.946 --> 14:45.448
He detests inefficiency more than anything in the world.

284
14:45.865 --> 14:48.535
Whenever you answer a question, answer him once.

285
14:48.618 --> 14:50.704
You detest inefficiency more than anything else.

286
14:51.955 --> 14:54.207
So do I, sir. And for that reason,

287
14:54.666 --> 14:56.668
as the person responsible for taking care of you,

288
14:57.127 --> 14:58.837
I'd like permission to look around your house.

289
14:58.920 --> 15:00.046
[gentle suspenseful music playing]

290
15:00.547 --> 15:01.506
Hmm.

291
15:07.887 --> 15:09.806
[gentle dramatic music playing]

292
15:10.014 --> 15:11.015
Whoa.

293
15:11.850 --> 15:13.101
[male employee 2] It's the Taekang Goddess.

294
15:13.184 --> 15:14.436
[male employee 3] It's her. It's really her!

295
15:14.519 --> 15:16.855
-She's glowing. -[gasps]

296
15:16.938 --> 15:18.022
Oh.

297
15:19.941 --> 15:21.234
[male employee 4] The Taekang Goddess.

298
15:21.818 --> 15:24.070
She's the stuff of legend. Okay.

299
15:24.154 --> 15:25.572
[elevator chimes]

300
15:41.588 --> 15:43.715
What's the status on Mr. Yoon's new secretary?

301
15:44.257 --> 15:45.467
Isn't she starting today?

302
15:48.428 --> 15:50.346
Yes, I believe so.

303
15:50.430 --> 15:52.390
I imagine he wants someone like Ms. Han.

304
15:52.682 --> 15:55.101
Who knows? I don't wanna assume anything.

305
15:55.685 --> 15:56.686
That's personal.

306
15:57.979 --> 16:00.482
I heard the VIPs will be in the chairman's office today.

307
16:00.815 --> 16:01.691
Do you know who?

308
16:03.526 --> 16:04.527
Who knows?

309
16:05.612 --> 16:07.030
I don't wanna assume anything.

310
16:07.322 --> 16:08.364
That's personal.

311
16:09.032 --> 16:10.366
Hmm.

312
16:16.372 --> 16:18.124
[Jae-hee] Yoon Yi-jun.

313
16:18.208 --> 16:21.920
I'm gonna have to build a friendly rapport with this total whack job.

314
16:22.170 --> 16:23.171
[sighs]

315
16:23.671 --> 16:25.089
Fine.

316
16:26.132 --> 16:29.552
Hmm? What's this?

317
16:30.094 --> 16:32.347
[pensive music playing]

318
16:32.806 --> 16:34.057
[sighs]

319
16:38.812 --> 16:39.938
[Wan-gu] From what her family said,

320
16:40.021 --> 16:43.233
there's a high possibility that someone hid Han Eun-young's phone.

321
16:47.987 --> 16:50.031
[Jae-hee] Where's that missing phone?

322
16:50.114 --> 16:52.242
The forensics team didn't find it on the scene.

323
16:52.826 --> 16:54.118
It could be somewhere inside.

324
16:55.286 --> 16:56.913
-[Yi-jun] What are you doing? -[musical sting whooshes]

325
16:57.455 --> 16:58.456
[gasps]

326
17:00.416 --> 17:01.668
[sighs]

327
17:01.918 --> 17:03.086
Why are you out here, sir?

328
17:03.169 --> 17:05.839
I was watching to see if you were slacking on the job.

329
17:07.173 --> 17:08.341
[sighs]

330
17:08.424 --> 17:10.385
What exactly have you heard?

331
17:10.468 --> 17:12.262
You're obviously playing dumb.

332
17:12.595 --> 17:15.098
[tense music playing]

333
17:15.181 --> 17:18.518
I heard there was a murder and that you've come under suspicion, sir.

334
17:18.601 --> 17:20.353
And knowing this, you wanted to work here?

335
17:21.521 --> 17:24.732
Unlike Mr. Chung, who immediately hightailed it out of here.

336
17:26.234 --> 17:27.235
So aren't you scared?

337
17:28.444 --> 17:29.779
I'm just curious.

338
17:29.863 --> 17:32.657
-Curious? -[tense music continues]

339
17:32.740 --> 17:34.659
What exactly are you so curious about, huh?

340
17:36.202 --> 17:40.123
Are you wondering whether I murdered my own secretary…

341
17:40.248 --> 17:42.375
and whether the rumors are true…

342
17:42.458 --> 17:46.004
and I really am a psychopathic homicidal maniac?

343
17:46.546 --> 17:47.547
[tense music continues]

344
17:48.256 --> 17:49.257
Neither.

345
17:50.884 --> 17:53.177
I just wanna know why you hired someone new.

346
17:53.261 --> 17:54.220
Why?

347
17:55.096 --> 17:56.806
The timing seems a bit weird.

348
17:57.599 --> 18:01.394
[tense music continues]

349
18:01.603 --> 18:02.604
Move backward.

350
18:03.646 --> 18:05.273
Huh?

351
18:13.990 --> 18:17.076
Number one of the three rules my personal secretary must abide by:

352
18:17.160 --> 18:18.328
act and speak efficiently.

353
18:18.411 --> 18:19.329
Second rule:

354
18:19.412 --> 18:21.956
maintain an appropriate physical and emotional distance.

355
18:22.040 --> 18:22.874
[sighs]

356
18:22.957 --> 18:26.336
Of course, I can cross that boundary whenever I want to,

357
18:26.669 --> 18:28.379
and you'll just have to deal with it.

358
18:29.047 --> 18:31.633
-But if you cross the boundary… -[tense music continues]

359
18:31.716 --> 18:34.344
[Jae-hee] Did Han Eun-young cross that boundary?

360
18:34.427 --> 18:36.804
Is that why you killed her?

361
18:43.186 --> 18:44.354
[Yi-jun] For your glasses.

362
18:45.146 --> 18:47.649
-Oh, no, that's all right. -Go get some decent ones.

363
18:48.983 --> 18:49.984
[Jae-hee] Oh.

364
18:53.947 --> 18:55.281
God, he's crazy.

365
18:56.074 --> 18:57.116
[groaning sigh]

366
18:58.910 --> 18:59.911
[tense rhythmic music playing]

367
19:01.120 --> 19:03.331
[Jae-hee] Han Eun-young was nowhere to be seen

368
19:03.414 --> 19:05.667
in the dash cam footage Yi-jun handed over.

369
19:06.417 --> 19:09.420
[tense rhythmic music continues]

370
19:11.381 --> 19:13.925
[Jae-hee] But what if he intentionally left out

371
19:14.008 --> 19:15.343
footage from one of his vehicles?

372
19:23.518 --> 19:24.727
[eerie musical sting]

373
19:24.811 --> 19:26.062
[gasps] Oh, damn it.

374
19:28.272 --> 19:29.649
You're different, that's for sure.

375
19:30.942 --> 19:32.610
You swear like a sailor.

376
19:32.694 --> 19:35.780
-Just trying to do my job, sir. -I know.

377
19:35.863 --> 19:38.491
-Though it seems performative. -[sighs]

378
19:38.574 --> 19:41.786
I'm sure they told you during training, I don't trust people.

379
19:42.245 --> 19:44.205
I'll always be keeping an eye on you,

380
19:44.706 --> 19:47.166
which means you have to keep proving yourself.

381
19:47.250 --> 19:48.418
For how long?

382
19:49.085 --> 19:50.253
Will you trust me eventually?

383
19:50.336 --> 19:51.713
That all depends.

384
19:53.214 --> 19:55.800
Now, for the final rule I have for my personal secretary,

385
19:56.592 --> 19:59.887
there's one room that you may not enter under any circumstances.

386
20:00.805 --> 20:03.808
-Where is it? So I can avoid it. -[tense music playing]

387
20:05.852 --> 20:08.021
[Yi-jun] Second floor, end of the hall on the left.

388
20:08.563 --> 20:09.897
Completely off limits.

389
20:10.440 --> 20:13.317
[Jae-hee] Okay. Second floor, end of the hall, left.

390
20:13.401 --> 20:14.527
That's the first place I'll--

391
20:14.694 --> 20:15.945
Oh…

392
20:19.323 --> 20:20.783
I sense you have a bad memory.

393
20:25.621 --> 20:26.622
[musical sting whooshing]

394
20:26.831 --> 20:29.250
-Move backward. -Oh.

395
20:30.543 --> 20:32.420
[yelps]

396
20:32.503 --> 20:36.549
[playful music playing]

397
20:45.516 --> 20:46.601
[Jerry meows]

398
20:46.684 --> 20:47.810
[growls]

399
20:49.020 --> 20:51.064
[gasps, grunts]

400
20:53.983 --> 20:55.443
[Jerry meows]

401
20:55.526 --> 20:57.028
[shouts]

402
20:59.447 --> 21:01.115
[Jae-hee whimpers] God, why are you so strong?

403
21:01.199 --> 21:02.158
[light playful music playing]

404
21:02.241 --> 21:03.868
[Si-hyun] Aw.

405
21:03.951 --> 21:05.661
Looks like they're getting along just fine.

406
21:06.704 --> 21:08.081
Look at you guys.

407
21:08.164 --> 21:11.125
-That didn't take long, did it? -Wow.

408
21:11.292 --> 21:12.835
[chuckles]

409
21:13.920 --> 21:16.255
Hi. Kim Si-hyun. I'm with his legal counsel.

410
21:16.881 --> 21:19.008
[Jae-hee] Yoon Yi-jun's right-hand man, Kim Si-hyun.

411
21:19.092 --> 21:20.301
Kang Jae-hee, new secretary.

412
21:21.302 --> 21:23.221
What an honor.

413
21:23.304 --> 21:25.890
I really get to touch the hand that slammed down Mr. Yoon.

414
21:25.973 --> 21:27.767
[laughs]

415
21:27.850 --> 21:29.811
-Who got slammed down? -Uh, you.

416
21:31.187 --> 21:33.022
-Who told you that? -Mr. Jung did.

417
21:33.231 --> 21:34.649
He heard it from the secretary's office.

418
21:34.732 --> 21:35.608
The sound really carried.

419
21:35.691 --> 21:38.152
I should have fired him before he had the chance to resign.

420
21:38.236 --> 21:39.862
[Si-hyun] I can't believe you did that with such tiny hands.

421
21:39.946 --> 21:41.572
-[Jae-hee] No, it was-- -It was part of an in-depth interview.

422
21:41.656 --> 21:42.657
[Jae-hee] But technically--

423
21:42.740 --> 21:44.867
I was trying to assess the inner depths of the interviewee's psyche--

424
21:44.992 --> 21:46.077
[Jae-hee] It's all about hip and core strength.

425
21:46.160 --> 21:47.245
-Are you even listening? -[Jae-hee] Like this.

426
21:47.328 --> 21:48.329
-[Si-hyun] Oh, the hips? -[Yi-jun] Hello?

427
21:48.412 --> 21:50.039
-What's that move? -[Jae-hee] Like this. I'll demonstrate.

428
21:50.123 --> 21:51.541
[Si-hyun] Oh. [grunts]

429
21:51.624 --> 21:53.876
[Jae-hee] Oh. You use your hip to carry your opponent's weight.

430
21:53.960 --> 21:55.545
-Hey. -[Si-hyun] Huh?

431
21:55.670 --> 21:57.380
You should pay attention. This is important, okay?

432
21:57.463 --> 21:58.840
-What next? -Oh, you got that?

433
21:58.965 --> 22:01.342
Oh. Whoa, that's great.

434
22:01.676 --> 22:03.553
So that's how you threw him over your shoulder.

435
22:07.974 --> 22:08.975
Hold on.

436
22:11.227 --> 22:12.353
Jerry?

437
22:12.436 --> 22:13.646
[Jerry meowing]

438
22:13.729 --> 22:16.649
Wait here with Mr. Special Forces, okay?

439
22:16.732 --> 22:18.025
[Jerry meowing]

440
22:23.906 --> 22:24.907
The study?

441
22:27.702 --> 22:31.497
[soft tense music playing]

442
22:32.123 --> 22:33.332
[door clicks]

443
22:33.416 --> 22:34.709
[Jerry growls]

444
22:35.710 --> 22:37.044
Don't you worry.

445
22:37.128 --> 22:40.965
I have no intention of bonding with your awful owner, whatsoever.

446
22:41.716 --> 22:43.968
You should feel free to hog every ounce of his affection.

447
22:44.635 --> 22:46.721
The man's all yours. Hmm?

448
22:46.804 --> 22:47.847
[Jerry meows]

449
22:53.311 --> 22:56.314
[tense music playing]

450
22:56.522 --> 22:59.317
The police submitted the post-mortem certificate,

451
22:59.400 --> 23:01.652
and Ms. Han's body is with her family now.

452
23:01.736 --> 23:02.778
[tense music continues]

453
23:02.987 --> 23:04.405
We've done all we can for them,

454
23:05.072 --> 23:06.699
and I've made them a generous offer,

455
23:07.950 --> 23:10.578
like you asked me to, which has sped things along.

456
23:13.080 --> 23:14.081
To think,

457
23:14.332 --> 23:15.625
[inhales]

458
23:15.750 --> 23:18.044
this entire situation was resolved so easily.

459
23:20.922 --> 23:21.797
[sighs]

460
23:21.881 --> 23:23.299
Kim Si-hyun must have had

461
23:23.382 --> 23:26.802
-an important reason to come all this way. -[porcelain clinking]

462
23:29.597 --> 23:31.015
You're going upstairs?

463
23:31.098 --> 23:33.935
-Yes. -I got this. I'll bring it up to him.

464
23:34.393 --> 23:35.978
Oh, uh, well, thank you.

465
23:36.062 --> 23:40.274
[laughs] Oh, and you might notice a door on the left down the hall.

466
23:40.358 --> 23:42.193
You shouldn't go in there. It's against the rules.

467
23:42.276 --> 23:43.194
Actually,

468
23:43.736 --> 23:47.198
-do you happen to know why it's that way? -[tense music playing]

469
23:47.782 --> 23:49.992
I just wanna know what I should be looking out for.

470
23:50.534 --> 23:52.995
Well, why should people like us be told?

471
23:53.496 --> 23:56.082
If they tell us something's off limits, that's that.

472
23:56.582 --> 23:58.417
[sighs] Thanks again.

473
23:58.501 --> 24:00.044
[chuckles]

474
24:00.127 --> 24:03.172
[tense music continues]

475
24:13.224 --> 24:15.309
[Jae-hee] Down the hall, second floor.

476
24:16.310 --> 24:18.646
[Yi-jun] There's one room that you may not enter

477
24:18.729 --> 24:19.647
under any circumstances.

478
24:22.692 --> 24:26.070
Second floor, end of the hall on the left.

479
24:27.029 --> 24:28.030
[Jae-hee] That's the one.

480
24:30.074 --> 24:31.534
[knocking]

481
24:31.617 --> 24:32.785
[Jae-hee] Mind if I come in?

482
24:40.876 --> 24:43.629
I see you're blatantly flouting my earlier instructions.

483
24:43.713 --> 24:44.922
[sighs]

484
24:45.006 --> 24:48.134
I know you said to wait. I didn't wanna be inhospitable.

485
24:48.301 --> 24:51.262
Day one on the job, and you're ignoring orders?

486
24:52.763 --> 24:53.848
Okay.

487
24:56.851 --> 24:57.852
That's enough.

488
24:58.519 --> 24:59.437
Take it back.

489
25:01.063 --> 25:03.691
Right. Sorry, sir. I'll take it back right away.

490
25:03.774 --> 25:06.736
Whoa, wait, I can take it. I'll drink it myself, geez.

491
25:06.819 --> 25:07.862
[chuckles]

492
25:08.362 --> 25:09.280
[whimsical squeak]

493
25:09.363 --> 25:10.448
I like it, all right?

494
25:11.365 --> 25:12.575
I'll stand by on the first floor.

495
25:15.828 --> 25:16.996
Hmm.

496
25:18.873 --> 25:20.458
[Si-hyun] What? Not thirsty?

497
25:21.000 --> 25:22.126
[pensive music playing]

498
25:22.543 --> 25:24.003
[Si-hyun] What's up with your lips?

499
25:24.086 --> 25:25.379
You rolled them back just now.

500
25:25.588 --> 25:27.798
-It's ugly. -[door clicks shut]

501
25:29.508 --> 25:30.593
[tense music playing]

502
25:30.718 --> 25:32.345
-[Si-hyun] That day-- -[gasps] It works.

503
25:32.428 --> 25:33.471
I can hear.

504
25:33.554 --> 25:34.972
[Si-hyun] about the thing Ms. Han saw.

505
25:35.890 --> 25:39.018
What's Mr. Park's status with the cleanup process?

506
25:39.810 --> 25:40.811
[Jae-hee] Mr. Park?

507
25:40.978 --> 25:44.106
You know, if Ms. Han hadn't seen anything,

508
25:44.857 --> 25:46.192
things would be different, huh?

509
25:46.275 --> 25:48.235
[liquid pouring]

510
25:48.319 --> 25:49.487
Han Eun-young?

511
25:51.155 --> 25:52.782
She saw something before she died?

512
25:54.241 --> 25:56.619
[Yi-jun] Yeah, well, what's done is done.

513
25:57.244 --> 25:58.662
Let's not rehash it all.

514
26:00.122 --> 26:01.248
[tense music continues]

515
26:01.457 --> 26:02.750
Guess it's pointless to think of that.

516
26:05.169 --> 26:06.212
How's the new secretary?

517
26:06.295 --> 26:08.381
-Do you like-- -[scoffs]

518
26:11.092 --> 26:12.510
Not at all.

519
26:12.593 --> 26:13.886
What's gotten into you, man?

520
26:13.969 --> 26:15.638
You replaced the last guy with this one.

521
26:16.972 --> 26:19.016
-He didn't have it. -Have what?

522
26:21.519 --> 26:23.521
A conscience. [sighs]

523
26:23.604 --> 26:24.772
[Yi-jun] That day at the parking lot,

524
26:25.231 --> 26:27.858
it was plain to see the deceased's family were the victims there,

525
26:28.526 --> 26:31.195
and still he sided against them to get on my good side.

526
26:31.278 --> 26:32.446
Isn't that what you wanted?

527
26:33.280 --> 26:35.324
[Si-hyun] You're ice cold, Yi-jun, seriously.

528
26:35.408 --> 26:38.494
-God, it's freezing in here. -Wow.

529
26:39.161 --> 26:40.621
Yoon Yi-jun's one scary guy.

530
26:41.497 --> 26:42.456
[case clacking]

531
26:43.916 --> 26:45.126
[door opens]

532
26:47.795 --> 26:49.046
[Si-hyun] I'll get going.

533
26:53.134 --> 26:54.260
Oh, that's right, Mr. Kang.

534
26:54.927 --> 26:56.679
You'll have to sign an official contract.

535
26:56.762 --> 26:58.514
Please forward us all your documents,

536
26:58.597 --> 27:01.642
-and know that I'm here to help you. -Ah, right. I appreciate it.

537
27:01.725 --> 27:03.519
-Mm. I'll talk to you soon. -[tense musical sting]

538
27:03.602 --> 27:05.438
Oh.

539
27:05.521 --> 27:07.356
That hurt. Ah.

540
27:07.648 --> 27:10.818
Oh, about the contract, you'll have to drop by Taekang HQ to sign it.

541
27:11.068 --> 27:13.320
-You'll do that? -Yes, that'll be fine.

542
27:19.702 --> 27:22.663
[soft pensive music playing]

543
27:30.838 --> 27:32.089
[tense percussive music playing]

544
27:32.298 --> 27:34.091
[Hye-jung] Taekang Retail CEO Yoon Mi-jin

545
27:34.175 --> 27:36.594
and Executive Director Yoon Na-jung are here for you, sir.

546
27:45.895 --> 27:46.896
[sighs]

547
27:47.730 --> 27:50.774
CHAIRMAN YOON TAE-SIK

548
28:01.785 --> 28:04.747
That promo video couldn't have been released at a better time,

549
28:05.206 --> 28:07.708
and Yi-jun's response was good. Public opinion's turned.

550
28:07.791 --> 28:09.668
He's such an attention hog.

551
28:10.085 --> 28:12.463
I guess that overseas tour wasn't enough for him.

552
28:14.715 --> 28:18.344
[sighs] It sounds like the rumors are dying down finally.

553
28:18.886 --> 28:21.555
It should all be sorted before you meet with the shareholders.

554
28:27.019 --> 28:28.562
-Ugh, that's hot. -[cup clinks]

555
28:28.646 --> 28:29.855
Hey!

556
28:30.731 --> 28:31.982
[Na-jung] One ice cube.

557
28:32.066 --> 28:33.734
Why don't you get it right for once?

558
28:37.112 --> 28:38.280
I'll get you another one.

559
28:40.574 --> 28:41.659
[scoffs]

560
28:41.742 --> 28:44.161
[Na-jung] You smile, but I know you're gonna go behind my back

561
28:44.245 --> 28:45.162
and say I'm a fucking tyrant.

562
28:45.246 --> 28:47.122
-That's enough. -[Na-jung] What?

563
28:47.206 --> 28:49.166
Rumors don't pop up on their own.

564
28:50.084 --> 28:52.086
There's always some kernel of truth in there.

565
28:53.379 --> 28:55.881
That dead secretary, for instance, really was involved

566
28:55.965 --> 28:58.717
with Yi-jun in some way, according to the rumors, that is.

567
28:59.426 --> 29:01.303
Just rumors. [laughs]

568
29:01.387 --> 29:02.763
[slams]

569
29:03.514 --> 29:04.515
[cup clinks]

570
29:05.516 --> 29:07.685
We're done. Everyone out.

571
29:07.768 --> 29:09.436
[tense dramatic music playing]

572
29:16.402 --> 29:19.530
So regardless of risks, he's gonna push through with the succession?

573
29:22.825 --> 29:24.368
[scoffs]

574
29:31.917 --> 29:35.045
[upbeat pop music playing]

575
29:40.009 --> 29:41.427
-Hmm. -Hmm.

576
29:42.469 --> 29:44.179
Hmm.

577
29:44.263 --> 29:47.141
There's that perfect fresh out of the oven delicate warmth.

578
29:47.224 --> 29:51.145
Superintendent Ma never understood it. Thank God we moved our meeting point here.

579
29:53.272 --> 29:56.734
Anyway, that Kim Si-hyun is no idiot. All my files check out?

580
29:56.817 --> 29:59.653
I'm getting a little confused. I thought I was the captain here,

581
29:59.737 --> 30:01.739
but now I feel like your lackey, you know?

582
30:01.822 --> 30:04.575
You're probably the only detective who makes her captain forge her papers.

583
30:05.284 --> 30:08.746
I have to sign a formal contract. What else do you expect me to do?

584
30:09.455 --> 30:11.123
Enough. Let's hear it.

585
30:11.206 --> 30:14.501
-What's Yi-jun like? What do you think? -Oh, the dude's completely insane.

586
30:15.002 --> 30:17.004
Two seconds with him makes me want to knock him out.

587
30:17.087 --> 30:19.715
The way he talks, he deserves a beating.

588
30:20.591 --> 30:21.550
Sounds like he's gonna get beaten.

589
30:22.092 --> 30:25.596
Just say the word, and I'll get right on that right away. [grunts]

590
30:25.679 --> 30:26.930
Whoa. Sit back down.

591
30:27.014 --> 30:29.475
You've got to rein it in. You're supposed to be his friend.

592
30:29.558 --> 30:31.810
This whole day has felt like military training, Captain,

593
30:32.019 --> 30:33.687
and I think I deserve a little credit.

594
30:33.771 --> 30:36.440
Oh, God. I told you, geez.

595
30:36.940 --> 30:39.026
Good job, Jae-hee. You're doing well.

596
30:39.109 --> 30:40.235
[sighs]

597
30:40.319 --> 30:41.654
Can I show you something hilarious?

598
30:41.737 --> 30:43.072
[sighs]

599
30:43.405 --> 30:45.115
This is for breaking my glasses.

600
30:46.325 --> 30:47.326
Hey, what…

601
30:47.618 --> 30:49.828
-Are these glasses inlaid with diamonds? -Whatever. Doesn't matter.

602
30:50.579 --> 30:51.872
Yi-jun wasn't at work on the 15th.

603
30:52.956 --> 30:55.167
-That's when the incident occurred. -[tense dramatic music playing]

604
30:57.586 --> 30:59.421
Han Eun-young apparently saw something.

605
31:00.589 --> 31:02.549
Sounds like she wasn't meant to hear it.

606
31:02.633 --> 31:05.344
But the first responders told us there wasn't any proof of that.

607
31:06.053 --> 31:07.971
There's a prick named Park who cleaned up after.

608
31:08.722 --> 31:09.723
Mr. Park?

609
31:11.225 --> 31:12.226
Oh.

610
31:12.893 --> 31:15.104
What about Mr. Jung? Was the infiltration successful?

611
31:15.312 --> 31:17.231
Uh-huh. He's the captain's hidden card.

612
31:18.232 --> 31:19.483
Your hidden card?

613
31:19.566 --> 31:20.943
Hm.

614
31:21.026 --> 31:22.861
[suspenseful synth music playing]

615
31:24.613 --> 31:27.157
[Wan-gu] Goddammit. Ace in the hole.

616
31:27.241 --> 31:28.492
Yeah, right, Park Bong-yi.

617
31:30.119 --> 31:33.122
[upbeat percussive music playing]

618
31:35.040 --> 31:37.167
Ugh, what am I even doing here?

619
31:37.251 --> 31:40.045
All they ever do is take a dump and then go.

620
31:40.796 --> 31:42.339
[sighs] I've had enough.

621
31:42.423 --> 31:43.924
[employee 1] Another all-nighter, huh?

622
31:44.007 --> 31:46.260
[employee 2] I know, right? It's like it never ends.

623
31:46.343 --> 31:48.595
-[groans] Ugh, I feel like death. -[spray bottle hisses]

624
31:49.638 --> 31:50.848
[employee 1] Hey, wanna go out for soju after?

625
31:50.931 --> 31:51.932
[employee 2] Okay.

626
31:52.850 --> 31:53.851
Hey,

627
31:54.601 --> 31:57.187
don't you get the feeling they're gonna axe Accounting Team Three soon?

628
31:58.647 --> 32:01.233
I mean, if even Mr. Yoon's nepo hire is nervous,

629
32:01.817 --> 32:03.277
everyone must be freaking out.

630
32:14.246 --> 32:15.873
So Park Min-hwan on team three.

631
32:16.248 --> 32:17.791
You notice how he never leaves his desk now?

632
32:18.333 --> 32:20.669
And he covers up his work whenever anyone comes by.

633
32:21.462 --> 32:22.421
[hisses]

634
32:22.796 --> 32:24.006
Could it be?

635
32:25.674 --> 32:26.675
What?

636
32:27.676 --> 32:28.761
[employee 2] You haven't heard?

637
32:28.844 --> 32:29.928
[suspenseful musical sting]

638
32:34.892 --> 32:37.895
[suspenseful dramatic music playing]

639
32:38.896 --> 32:41.607
[thunder booming]

640
32:42.691 --> 32:44.234
[gasps]

641
32:50.491 --> 32:51.492
[sighs]

642
32:58.665 --> 33:01.710
[tense music playing]

643
33:02.419 --> 33:03.504
[sighs]

644
33:10.177 --> 33:11.720
[loud clattering]

645
33:12.221 --> 33:15.557
[tense piano music playing]

646
33:21.980 --> 33:23.232
[rumbling eerie musical sting]

647
33:23.315 --> 33:24.900
[gasps]

648
33:24.983 --> 33:25.984
[glass shatters]

649
33:28.111 --> 33:29.613
[panting]

650
33:31.156 --> 33:34.326
[gasps]

651
33:39.998 --> 33:42.000
[Jae-hee] I just wanna know why you hired someone new.

652
33:42.417 --> 33:43.418
Why?

653
33:44.211 --> 33:45.546
The timing seems a bit weird.

654
34:04.940 --> 34:06.817
Whoa.

655
34:10.028 --> 34:11.864
-[clattering] -Ah. Oh, God.

656
34:11.947 --> 34:14.992
-Are you okay? -I'm so sorry. What a…

657
34:15.075 --> 34:17.536
-Oh, man, I totally spaced out. -You okay, miss?

658
34:19.788 --> 34:21.039
Kang Jae-hee?

659
34:22.416 --> 34:24.585
You're Mr. Yoon's new secretary, aren't you?

660
34:25.544 --> 34:26.545
Yes, that's right.

661
34:26.962 --> 34:28.463
Mr. Jang told me about you.

662
34:28.922 --> 34:31.049
I'm the chairman's secretary, Lee Hye-jung.

663
34:31.717 --> 34:33.135
Oh, nice to meet you.

664
34:34.511 --> 34:35.804
Nice to meet you.

665
34:36.471 --> 34:39.057
Thanks for that, a second ago.

666
34:43.103 --> 34:44.479
[Jae-hee] The chairman's secretary,

667
34:45.272 --> 34:46.189
Lee Hye-jung.

668
34:49.568 --> 34:51.653
What were you thinking? You made your life a lot harder.

669
34:52.029 --> 34:53.113
Oh, Mr. Kim.

670
34:53.196 --> 34:55.240
In the eyes of every man at Taekang's office,

671
34:55.449 --> 34:57.075
you're basically enemy number one.

672
34:57.784 --> 34:59.328
-Huh? -Can't you feel the glares?

673
34:59.703 --> 35:01.330
Ah. Oh, wow.

674
35:01.622 --> 35:03.749
Gosh, they're coming from all directions.

675
35:03.832 --> 35:05.667
[upbeat funky music playing]

676
35:07.127 --> 35:08.712
Are they staring right now?

677
35:08.879 --> 35:10.255
[inaudible dialogue]

678
35:15.677 --> 35:18.180
-Okay, let go. -[chuckles]

679
35:19.806 --> 35:20.724
You're a little tense.

680
35:23.435 --> 35:25.145
There's something you should know.

681
35:25.228 --> 35:28.982
You won't be part of the club until she's made you suffer. Just an FYI.

682
35:29.066 --> 35:32.694
The LRA club, that's the Lee Hye-jung Rejects Alliance for short. [laughs]

683
35:32.778 --> 35:35.864
Oh, I guess Miss Lee is quite popular.

684
35:35.948 --> 35:39.201
You have no idea. The numbers keep growing month after month,

685
35:39.284 --> 35:40.994
never slowing down. Why, you ask?

686
35:41.078 --> 35:43.580
It's because month after month she keeps rejecting them.

687
35:43.664 --> 35:46.041
[laughs] I don't know if you're interested in becoming a member,

688
35:46.124 --> 35:47.000
but you seem kind of clueless,

689
35:47.084 --> 35:49.503
so I wanted to fill you in on it. That's all. Mm.

690
35:49.586 --> 35:51.630
I'm gonna assume that you're also a member?

691
35:51.713 --> 35:52.839
[comical musical sting]

692
35:53.590 --> 35:54.883
[whimsical music playing]

693
35:55.092 --> 35:57.636
-Why do you assume? -So it's more of a secret crush then, huh?

694
35:57.719 --> 35:58.762
Seriously, where's this coming from?

695
35:59.805 --> 36:02.349
Do I look like someone who'd have a crush they'd never act on?

696
36:02.432 --> 36:05.519
[whimsical music continues]

697
36:05.727 --> 36:07.479
-Understood. -I can tell you don't understand.

698
36:07.896 --> 36:10.524
Why'd you pause, Mr. Kang? Hey, don't you look away.

699
36:11.233 --> 36:14.111
My pride is on the line here. I wanna be crystal clear.

700
36:15.404 --> 36:17.781
The Taekang Goddess is totally my type physically,

701
36:17.990 --> 36:20.784
but her personality sucks. Her perfection is suffocating.

702
36:20.867 --> 36:23.412
She's predictable and therefore, totally uninteresting.

703
36:23.996 --> 36:25.455
I don't understand why you're shaking your head.

704
36:25.539 --> 36:28.291
Am I not getting through to you? What?

705
36:28.375 --> 36:29.626
What?

706
36:30.085 --> 36:33.088
[playful jazzy music playing]

707
36:37.926 --> 36:40.303
Mr. Jang mentions you've never done this kind of work before.

708
36:40.679 --> 36:42.848
-Oh, right. -If you need help, get in touch.

709
36:44.224 --> 36:45.392
Thank you, miss.

710
36:46.143 --> 36:48.562
-Oh, and Mr. Kim. -Yes?

711
36:49.396 --> 36:52.315
You don't get to turn me down. I'm the one who turns you down.

712
36:52.733 --> 36:53.942
You're not my type at all.

713
36:54.568 --> 36:55.819
[gasps]

714
36:59.239 --> 37:00.991
-Stay strong, sir. -What do you mean?

715
37:01.074 --> 37:03.243
She didn't… she didn't turn me down.

716
37:03.326 --> 37:05.120
-That doesn't count. Hey, wait. -[phone buzzing]

717
37:06.830 --> 37:08.832
[Wan-gu] Emergency. Come to the men's bathroom

718
37:08.915 --> 37:10.083
farthest from the elevator.

719
37:18.467 --> 37:20.761
[Jae-hee] Hey, looks like you missed a spot there. Right there.

720
37:20.844 --> 37:22.387
-Oh, here? Got it. -Yeah.

721
37:22.929 --> 37:23.805
[Jae-hee] Get in there.

722
37:25.974 --> 37:27.517
You little… Stop messing around.

723
37:27.601 --> 37:28.810
-[Jae-hee] Oh. -[Wan-gu gasps] Crap.

724
37:28.894 --> 37:31.146
Ah. Hey, you shouldn't lean against a urinal.

725
37:31.229 --> 37:32.814
-Ugh. -I just finished cleaning it.

726
37:32.898 --> 37:35.317
-I'm glad that's the reason it's wet. -Ah, whatever.

727
37:35.859 --> 37:37.944
I thought you told me I'm supposed to act like I don't know you,

728
37:38.070 --> 37:39.863
-so why did you wanna meet up? -Shh.

729
37:43.992 --> 37:46.161
You said Eun-young might have stumbled onto something,

730
37:46.244 --> 37:47.662
judging from the conversation you heard.

731
37:48.747 --> 37:51.291
Yes. I've already talked to you about this.

732
37:51.458 --> 37:52.459
I'm leaving.

733
37:53.585 --> 37:55.837
[tense music playing]

734
37:56.046 --> 37:57.756
There's one more thing.

735
37:57.923 --> 37:59.424
THE DAY OF THE INCIDENT FEBRUARY 5TH, LATE AT NIGHT

736
37:59.508 --> 38:00.425
[elevator chimes]

737
38:00.509 --> 38:03.053
[tense rhythmic music playing]

738
38:03.136 --> 38:05.180
Oh, Mr. Park.

739
38:05.263 --> 38:06.473
Ah, Mr. Ha.

740
38:07.808 --> 38:10.727
ACCOUNTING TEAM 3 MANAGER PARK MIN-HWAN

741
38:11.186 --> 38:12.395
I thought you'd already gone home.

742
38:12.729 --> 38:14.940
Oh, not yet. Heading out now.

743
38:19.736 --> 38:21.071
[elevator chimes]

744
38:21.446 --> 38:24.157
[Wan-gu] The manager of Accounting Team Three, Park Min-hwan,

745
38:24.366 --> 38:26.660
carried a bunch of stuff out of Yoon Yi-jun's office

746
38:26.743 --> 38:28.620
before the first responders arrived.

747
38:29.246 --> 38:32.999
-He ran into an employee on his way out. -[tense rhythmic music continues]

748
38:33.083 --> 38:36.044
We missed it because the CCTVs were undergoing maintenance.

749
38:42.759 --> 38:45.470
[Captain Park] So we're thinking that Yoon Yi-jun killed Han Eun-young

750
38:45.971 --> 38:47.347
because she found something out,

751
38:48.181 --> 38:50.016
and Park Min-hwan cleaned up the scene,

752
38:50.725 --> 38:55.272
making off with the damning evidence. Hmm. Everything lines up.

753
38:56.189 --> 38:57.315
Anything on Park Min-hwan?

754
38:57.399 --> 38:59.442
He's an accounting manager Yi-jun hired while studying abroad.

755
38:59.526 --> 39:01.820
He was always with him and Si-hyun. That's all I found out.

756
39:01.903 --> 39:02.821
Hmm.

757
39:03.905 --> 39:05.699
For the time being, we'll watch Min-hwan's movements.

758
39:06.241 --> 39:09.327
We'll try to slowly suffocate him. The missing phone is the key here.

759
39:09.411 --> 39:11.037
[resonant percussive hit]

760
39:14.958 --> 39:17.627
[suspenseful percussive music playing]

761
39:25.260 --> 39:27.387
Don't mind him. He's been in a bad mood.

762
39:28.096 --> 39:29.055
Oh, something wrong?

763
39:29.139 --> 39:31.016
He's always like this when he doesn't sleep enough.

764
39:31.183 --> 39:33.685
[scoffs] It's happening a lot recently.

765
39:33.768 --> 39:36.563
[tense atmospheric music playing]

766
39:48.992 --> 39:50.202
Hello, Mr. Yoon.

767
39:51.369 --> 39:54.164
The reason I'm late is because I had to give Mr. Kim my documents.

768
39:55.498 --> 39:58.168
[Jae-hee] Why, what is it? What's bothering you this time?

769
39:58.251 --> 39:59.461
Huh?

770
40:02.088 --> 40:04.049
Oh, are you the one who moved this?

771
40:04.466 --> 40:06.009
Why is it positioned like that?

772
40:06.092 --> 40:07.344
[light inquisitive music playing]

773
40:07.427 --> 40:08.511
Then you noticed it?

774
40:09.346 --> 40:11.139
-Well? -Yes.

775
40:11.806 --> 40:15.185
I could've sworn that yesterday when I put it down,

776
40:16.144 --> 40:17.687
it was like this, not like that.

777
40:17.771 --> 40:18.855
[dramatic percussive sting]

778
40:19.064 --> 40:20.065
Come here.

779
40:22.067 --> 40:23.693
Quickly.

780
40:23.777 --> 40:27.155
[upbeat percussive music playing]

781
40:30.367 --> 40:32.953
The lights seem dimmer than they were before I left yesterday.

782
40:33.453 --> 40:35.997
It seems to be a lot darker in here now. I'm almost sure of it.

783
40:36.081 --> 40:37.707
So I'm not the only one to notice it?

784
40:38.959 --> 40:40.919
There you go. I'm not going insane.

785
40:41.670 --> 40:42.879
I knew I wasn't crazy.

786
40:47.133 --> 40:48.134
I'm hungry.

787
40:48.760 --> 40:50.178
I'm gonna go eat now.

788
40:53.682 --> 40:55.976
[crowd murmuring]

789
40:58.395 --> 40:59.354
[sighs]

790
40:59.437 --> 41:02.565
Oh. The Taekang Goddess rejected him yesterday.

791
41:03.400 --> 41:06.111
[gasps] No way, she's here. It's her right there.

792
41:06.528 --> 41:09.364
Oh, no, Mr. Cho. Are you gonna be okay?

793
41:09.447 --> 41:11.283
[Mr. Cho] I… I should, uh, probably go now.

794
41:11.366 --> 41:12.242
[chuckles]

795
41:24.379 --> 41:25.547
Miji.

796
41:25.630 --> 41:27.549
[soft intriguing music playing]

797
41:27.632 --> 41:30.677
Everyone's saying how handsome he is. So are the rumors true?

798
41:31.303 --> 41:33.847
I guess, not exactly.

799
41:34.055 --> 41:35.307
I thought he was pretty.

800
41:35.390 --> 41:39.352
Oh, a hanpty man, the combination of handsome and pretty.

801
41:40.687 --> 41:43.273
And with that, the dreamboat holy trinity is complete.

802
41:44.065 --> 41:45.900
Yoon Yi-jun, Kim Si-hyun, and Kang Jae-hee.

803
41:46.818 --> 41:50.155
-You've memorized his name already? -Though Mr. Yoon's my choice.

804
41:50.363 --> 41:52.782
Which of the three would you choose?

805
41:55.118 --> 41:56.244
[whimsical music playing]

806
41:56.453 --> 41:57.329
[Si-hyun] Miji,

807
41:58.371 --> 41:59.456
I'm sorry about earlier.

808
41:59.914 --> 42:01.291
That was rude.

809
42:01.374 --> 42:03.126
[lighthearted upbeat music playing]

810
42:04.002 --> 42:05.337
[sighs]

811
42:06.546 --> 42:07.547
I'm sorry.

812
42:17.432 --> 42:20.226
[Jae-hee] What did you say? Are you being serious?

813
42:21.269 --> 42:23.646
Completely serious, 100%.

814
42:23.730 --> 42:26.649
This should tell you that I'm starting to trust you.

815
42:26.733 --> 42:29.152
What on earth does trusting me have to do with this situation?

816
42:29.611 --> 42:30.487
Actually, a lot.

817
42:30.987 --> 42:33.823
Since my secretary's confirmed that I'm of sound mind,

818
42:34.574 --> 42:36.743
shouldn't he trust whatever I throw his way?

819
42:37.243 --> 42:38.244
Starting today,

820
42:39.037 --> 42:41.164
your role is to keep me safe.

821
42:41.247 --> 42:43.666
But I'm already next to you day in and day out.

822
42:44.125 --> 42:45.710
What more can I do to ensure your safety?

823
42:46.336 --> 42:47.337
You'll protect my health.

824
42:47.796 --> 42:48.797
You're saying…

825
42:49.798 --> 42:51.341
you want me to be a food taster?

826
42:51.424 --> 42:53.093
[soft tense music playing]

827
42:53.593 --> 42:54.928
That's not in my contract.

828
42:55.345 --> 42:58.264
You'll be given an additional 200% in hazard pay.

829
42:58.348 --> 43:00.809
You think I'll do anything for money, right?

830
43:00.892 --> 43:02.602
Actually, that's exactly what I think.

831
43:03.520 --> 43:05.105
You think your food's poisoned.

832
43:05.188 --> 43:08.024
I heard Miss Choi has been cooking meals for you for over a decade.

833
43:08.108 --> 43:09.359
I thought I'd explained this.

834
43:09.442 --> 43:12.028
I have next to no trust in people, only situations.

835
43:12.112 --> 43:14.030
If you won't taste it, then go.

836
43:14.114 --> 43:15.490
[swishing]

837
43:17.742 --> 43:18.910
[sighs]

838
43:23.081 --> 43:24.124
[sighs]

839
43:30.088 --> 43:32.924
[jaunty upbeat music playing]

840
43:35.176 --> 43:36.219
What, are you crazy?

841
43:40.598 --> 43:42.016
Who tastes someone's food like that?

842
43:42.809 --> 43:44.436
What if it was poisoned after all?

843
43:51.985 --> 43:52.944
It could be quite dangerous.

844
43:54.821 --> 43:56.823
Fine, go ahead. Eat it all.

845
44:02.203 --> 44:04.205
[tense dramatic music playing]

846
44:06.458 --> 44:07.917
[gasps, chokes]

847
44:08.001 --> 44:09.335
[gasps, chokes]

848
44:09.419 --> 44:10.712
I knew it was poisonous!

849
44:10.795 --> 44:12.380
Stay back. [gasping]

850
44:12.464 --> 44:13.423
What was in it?

851
44:14.215 --> 44:16.301
-What's in it? -[gasping] Dude.

852
44:16.384 --> 44:18.803
What is it, what'd they put in it? What's wrong with it?

853
44:20.013 --> 44:24.392
-Come on, tell me. What is it? -[gasping] The food.

854
44:25.643 --> 44:28.521
-What? Come on. -The food tastes like crap, sir.

855
44:28.605 --> 44:30.523
[record scratch]

856
44:30.607 --> 44:32.358
Man, that wasn't a tasting, that was pure torture.

857
44:32.442 --> 44:33.735
Oh.

858
44:33.818 --> 44:35.028
How can you eat this stuff?

859
44:35.111 --> 44:38.531
That stuff contains Guérande salt, Tuscan olive oil.

860
44:38.615 --> 44:40.742
-Ugh. -It has Madagascan wild peppers.

861
44:40.825 --> 44:42.577
I don't care about that stuff.

862
44:43.119 --> 44:45.079
I refuse to eat food like that.

863
44:48.791 --> 44:49.834
If I'm gonna taste it,

864
44:50.793 --> 44:52.253
I'll use my way.

865
44:52.337 --> 44:54.172
[upbeat music playing]

866
44:58.551 --> 45:02.013
[funky upbeat music playing]

867
45:03.056 --> 45:04.307
Ugh.

868
45:05.600 --> 45:06.643
[sighs]

869
45:09.437 --> 45:11.606
Doesn't it kind of defeat the point

870
45:11.689 --> 45:13.274
if you mix everything together like that?

871
45:13.816 --> 45:14.817
Mm.

872
45:15.026 --> 45:17.111
Oh, gosh. [groans]

873
45:19.739 --> 45:21.699
[hums appreciatively]

874
45:22.283 --> 45:23.993
Nothing wrong with it. Do you want some of that?

875
45:24.077 --> 45:25.537
-No, I will not. -No?

876
45:29.374 --> 45:30.375
[phone buzzing]

877
45:31.125 --> 45:33.753
-[gasps] -[phone buzzing]

878
45:36.881 --> 45:38.716
-[Jae-hee] Park Min-hwan. -[tense dramatic music playing]

879
45:39.551 --> 45:42.804
Do you think Park Min-hwan might have handled the cleanup?

880
45:43.680 --> 45:46.057
Hmm, in movies, you know, when they do a cleanup,

881
45:46.558 --> 45:48.810
the elite criminals always make their lackeys do it.

882
45:49.644 --> 45:52.438
-He's here, sir. -[Captain Park] Whoa.

883
45:52.522 --> 45:54.524
[grunts]

884
45:54.607 --> 45:55.817
[car alarm beeps]

885
45:59.153 --> 46:00.238
-[car door closes] -[engine starts]

886
46:04.200 --> 46:05.201
[gasps]

887
46:05.285 --> 46:06.661
[Captain Park] Hey, Dong, stop the car.

888
46:06.744 --> 46:09.622
-Is he gone? Go, go, go. -He's starting, let's start. Let's go.

889
46:09.706 --> 46:13.001
[pensive music playing]

890
46:20.800 --> 46:22.343
[Seok-jin] Damn it. Where is he going?

891
46:22.427 --> 46:24.220
His house is in the opposite direction. Huh?

892
46:24.304 --> 46:25.805
Where is he going?

893
46:25.888 --> 46:27.557
Naon Art Center, I think.

894
46:27.932 --> 46:28.933
Naon Art Center.

895
46:29.851 --> 46:30.852
I know I've heard of it.

896
46:35.898 --> 46:36.899
[pensive music continues]

897
46:37.108 --> 46:39.444
Hey, try to catch up. Change lanes. Follow closely.

898
46:39.527 --> 46:40.820
-[car honking] -[yelps]

899
46:42.572 --> 46:43.615
What's with that guy?

900
46:43.698 --> 46:44.574
[sighs]

901
46:49.370 --> 46:51.122
You got your work cut out for you, huh?

902
46:51.205 --> 46:52.915
You've got more work than I do, Myung-suk.

903
46:53.833 --> 46:55.418
No complaints as long as I get paid for it.

904
46:56.461 --> 46:58.212
Mr. Yoon's always been like this.

905
46:58.296 --> 47:00.840
He complains about his food. He's a very picky eater.

906
47:00.923 --> 47:02.592
[sighs]

907
47:03.009 --> 47:06.596
You should try thinking of him as a fussy little kid. [laughs]

908
47:17.815 --> 47:20.818
[tense music playing]

909
47:41.547 --> 47:42.965
[Yi-jun] I won't need you.

910
47:43.841 --> 47:44.717
Wait in the car.

911
48:00.108 --> 48:03.111
[suspenseful music playing]

912
48:11.703 --> 48:12.745
Oh.

913
48:15.456 --> 48:16.916
Maybe we should have met at your house, sir.

914
48:16.999 --> 48:18.584
The CCTVs.

915
48:18.668 --> 48:20.253
I needed to check something.

916
48:20.628 --> 48:24.090
Stop looking down. I turned the CCTVs off. You look suspicious that way.

917
48:25.341 --> 48:26.843
[Min-hwan] Oh.

918
48:26.926 --> 48:28.344
[chuckles softly] Uh, what about the director?

919
48:29.178 --> 48:30.888
Paris on business,

920
48:30.972 --> 48:35.852
which means no one knows you're here except for me, Mr. Park.

921
48:40.898 --> 48:43.651
Everything she saw has been disposed of?

922
48:45.361 --> 48:46.696
Yes, of course, sir.

923
48:47.405 --> 48:49.490
Find somewhere to lie low for a while.

924
49:02.086 --> 49:05.089
[tense ominous music playing]

925
49:17.185 --> 49:21.105
[grunts, pants]

926
49:27.445 --> 49:29.947
I think I remember telling you to stay in the car.

927
49:30.531 --> 49:32.867
Let me think of a few possible reasons you're in here.

928
49:33.117 --> 49:37.205
Number one, you had to use the bathroom. Number two, you got lost after.

929
49:37.288 --> 49:39.665
Number three, you're following me for some reason.

930
49:41.292 --> 49:42.460
I think I know the answer,

931
49:42.543 --> 49:44.504
but I'm getting the feeling, Mr. Special Forces,

932
49:44.879 --> 49:46.547
you might just be inclined to lie.

933
49:47.590 --> 49:48.591
What have you got to say?

934
49:52.845 --> 49:54.972
Third one. Following you.

935
49:55.807 --> 49:58.059
Who are you? Who sent you?

936
49:58.476 --> 50:01.103
-[gasps] -[tense ominous music continues]

937
50:02.730 --> 50:04.023
[pants]

938
50:04.649 --> 50:08.152
[panting]

939
50:09.612 --> 50:12.532
-Which news outlet are you with? -[gasps]

940
50:12.615 --> 50:14.826
-You're in big trouble, mister. -[grunts]

941
50:27.797 --> 50:30.299
I saw him in the parking lot. He seemed suspicious, sir.

942
50:32.718 --> 50:33.970
I'll review the footage.

943
50:35.054 --> 50:37.098
-Or would you like me to-- -Forget it.

944
50:39.559 --> 50:40.768
Wait in the car.

945
50:45.648 --> 50:47.066
I'll review the footage myself.

946
50:56.075 --> 50:59.287
[car engine humming]

947
51:01.873 --> 51:05.459
[tense music playing]

948
51:33.237 --> 51:35.615
[upbeat electronic music playing]

949
51:38.784 --> 51:39.952
[tires screeching]

950
51:49.420 --> 51:51.714
[woman] Cheers. Congratulations.

951
51:51.797 --> 51:54.425
-[Si-hyun] Take two, huh? -[laughing]

952
51:54.842 --> 51:56.469
[woman] Man, you really wanna get remarried

953
51:56.552 --> 51:58.554
after all the trouble of getting divorced?

954
51:58.638 --> 51:59.805
Of course.

955
52:00.222 --> 52:01.724
'Cause it wasn't like this with the ex.

956
52:02.266 --> 52:03.559
[man] I've got a gut feeling this time.

957
52:03.643 --> 52:05.978
I know she's the one. Come on, guys.

958
52:06.062 --> 52:09.607
You should celebrate with us. Let's go. Especially you, Kim Si-hyun.

959
52:09.690 --> 52:10.816
[laughs]

960
52:10.900 --> 52:14.236
Wow, the divorce lawyer suddenly in favor of matrimony.

961
52:14.320 --> 52:16.197
Worlds really are colliding, huh? [laughs]

962
52:16.280 --> 52:18.491
How long are you gonna keep up the Kim Si-hyun act?

963
52:19.116 --> 52:20.242
Forever?

964
52:20.326 --> 52:21.535
[laughs]

965
52:21.619 --> 52:22.954
So you're gonna say yes to every girl,

966
52:23.037 --> 52:25.748
have a good time with her, and then send her on her way?

967
52:26.415 --> 52:27.583
Where's that gonna lead you?

968
52:28.125 --> 52:31.420
When you're dealing with a case that you really know won't be a slam dunk,

969
52:31.921 --> 52:33.297
it's always best to settle.

970
52:33.381 --> 52:35.549
That's how I view my lifestyle. I've just settled.

971
52:35.633 --> 52:37.134
-Let's drink. -[man 2] Mm-hmm.

972
52:37.218 --> 52:38.761
-Congrats. -Congrats.

973
52:38.844 --> 52:40.596
Thanks, guys. Cheers.

974
52:41.305 --> 52:42.974
[phone buzzing]

975
52:43.391 --> 52:44.392
Be right back.

976
52:45.518 --> 52:46.602
Hey, buddy.

977
52:48.104 --> 52:50.314
-About Mr. Special Forces. -[Si-hyun] Uh-huh.

978
52:50.690 --> 52:51.691
I'm wondering,

979
52:53.818 --> 52:56.904
-his contract, he signed off? -Uh-huh. Why?

980
52:57.363 --> 52:58.364
Is that really why you're calling?

981
52:59.407 --> 53:02.827
-[Yi-jun] Well, actually, Mr. Kang… -[upbeat club music playing]

982
53:02.910 --> 53:04.829
Hey, what's… what's with all the noise?

983
53:05.830 --> 53:08.582
-Anyway, just in case. -I gotta go.

984
53:08.666 --> 53:10.960
Special Forc… You there? Hello?

985
53:12.003 --> 53:13.421
He really hung up?

986
53:14.922 --> 53:16.215
[sighs]

987
53:19.635 --> 53:21.595
[tense music playing]

988
53:23.139 --> 53:24.265
It's fine.

989
53:25.516 --> 53:27.727
Anyone in my shoes would've gotten it wrong as well.

990
53:32.940 --> 53:36.318
[upbeat electronic music playing]

991
54:00.342 --> 54:03.220
[electronic music continues]

992
54:24.575 --> 54:28.079
You said I'm too boring for you, plus I already turned you down.

993
54:28.621 --> 54:31.540
So let's just move on, act like we're strangers.

994
54:32.666 --> 54:34.001
Wait.

995
54:37.004 --> 54:38.339
I think I've seen too much to move on.

996
54:39.465 --> 54:42.134
You've shattered my preconceptions. Are you the Miji I know?

997
54:42.510 --> 54:44.845
You sure you're not her sister or maybe mother?

998
54:45.387 --> 54:46.388
[chuckles]

999
54:47.014 --> 54:49.391
If you wanna pretend we're strangers, we should commit to that.

1000
54:49.475 --> 54:52.311
But if you wanna dance, let's hit the floor.

1001
54:52.394 --> 54:54.730
I hate guys who don't commit, as you'll find out.

1002
54:56.065 --> 54:58.442
-[gulps] -[glass clinks]

1003
55:00.111 --> 55:03.197
[upbeat electronic music playing]

1004
55:29.974 --> 55:33.352
[electronic music playing]

1005
55:35.312 --> 55:37.356
[sighs] Wow.

1006
55:37.439 --> 55:40.776
Suspect or not, that guy's an unusually despicable human being.

1007
55:41.318 --> 55:43.571
His sole existence makes me believe in evil.

1008
55:43.779 --> 55:45.865
-You did well. -[sighs]

1009
55:45.948 --> 55:46.949
I looked into it.

1010
55:47.366 --> 55:50.911
That guy wasn't there covering a show, and he wasn't tipped off by police.

1011
55:51.245 --> 55:52.246
Who was he then?

1012
55:53.164 --> 55:55.749
Ugh, if the press gets wind of this, that'll make this really hard.

1013
55:56.375 --> 55:58.460
And Yi-jun? He believed you?

1014
55:58.544 --> 56:01.463
Oh, given the situation, I think he bought it.

1015
56:02.089 --> 56:03.090
Whoever that reporter was,

1016
56:03.174 --> 56:04.466
he's the main reason my cover wasn't blown.

1017
56:05.009 --> 56:07.386
What about Park Min-hwan?

1018
56:07.803 --> 56:10.139
He's definitely involved, judging by the way they made contact.

1019
56:11.640 --> 56:14.518
The Captain wants us to find dirt on him so we can corner him first.

1020
56:15.269 --> 56:17.146
The phone. You think you can find it soon?

1021
56:17.771 --> 56:18.772
There's this place.

1022
56:19.440 --> 56:21.609
It's a room on the second floor that I was told is off limits.

1023
56:22.359 --> 56:24.445
I'll look there tomorrow. I'll get inside somehow.

1024
56:24.528 --> 56:25.529
Okay.

1025
56:32.119 --> 56:33.329
I noticed while getting a drink.

1026
56:34.914 --> 56:35.915
Your button.

1027
56:40.586 --> 56:42.046
Thank you. I appreciate it.

1028
56:42.129 --> 56:44.173
[gentle music playing]

1029
56:48.344 --> 56:49.511
[Si-hyun] I know, right?

1030
56:50.596 --> 56:52.681
-[Hye-jung] It's kinda cold. -[Si-hyun] You have that.

1031
56:53.224 --> 56:54.141
[Hye-jung] It's not that cold.

1032
56:54.225 --> 56:56.560
-Oh, want me to carry that? -Okay, thanks.

1033
56:57.019 --> 56:58.604
[scoffs] No problem.

1034
56:59.980 --> 57:03.067
[gentle poignant music playing]

1035
57:04.526 --> 57:09.031
♪ Say all the things you keep from me ♪

1036
57:09.990 --> 57:14.536
♪ I don't know why I smile anymore ♪

1037
57:15.704 --> 57:20.251
♪ How is it that you make me feel alive? ♪

1038
57:21.293 --> 57:26.465
♪ You look at me like no one before ♪

1039
57:26.548 --> 57:31.637
♪ This high has kept me from feeling low ♪

1040
57:32.388 --> 57:34.974
♪ I don't wanna let you go ♪

1041
57:35.057 --> 57:37.518
♪ I don't feel it anymore ♪

1042
57:37.601 --> 57:41.772
♪ I wanna be at your place tonight ♪

1043
57:43.357 --> 57:45.192
♪ You're the one to let me go ♪

1044
57:46.235 --> 57:49.363
♪ I'm slowly falling into your eyes ♪

1045
58:00.124 --> 58:02.376
[gentle poignant music continues]

1046
58:11.093 --> 58:12.720
[latch clicks]

1047
58:17.266 --> 58:18.684
[sighs]

1048
58:19.852 --> 58:21.562
[Jae-hee] I don't wanna go in there.

1049
58:22.271 --> 58:23.564
[sighs]

1050
58:26.817 --> 58:29.945
Second floor, end of hall. I'll get in, no matter what happens.

1051
58:31.613 --> 58:33.741
[Ms. Choi] Oh, gosh, please be more careful with those.

1052
58:34.116 --> 58:35.701
These trees are very expensive.

1053
58:36.660 --> 58:38.620
Goodness. [laughs]

1054
58:38.704 --> 58:40.497
Oh, Mr. Kang, you're here.

1055
58:41.040 --> 58:42.291
Mr. Yoon hasn't gotten up yet.

1056
58:42.666 --> 58:44.335
Doesn't sound like he slept well last night either.

1057
58:44.418 --> 58:45.627
Should I check on him?

1058
58:45.961 --> 58:47.087
Oh, right.

1059
58:47.171 --> 58:49.715
Would you mind bringing him the water and vegetable juice I prepared?

1060
58:50.549 --> 58:52.343
I meant to leave it in his bedroom earlier.

1061
58:52.551 --> 58:54.887
Things have just been so hectic today with all this cleaning.

1062
58:54.970 --> 58:57.264
It's no problem at all. I'll get on that.

1063
58:57.681 --> 58:59.767
I'll just be here on standby anyway. I'll take care of it.

1064
59:00.559 --> 59:02.061
Thank you, Mr. Kang.

1065
59:02.144 --> 59:03.187
[laughs]

1066
59:03.729 --> 59:05.105
Hey.

1067
59:05.189 --> 59:07.983
Oh, the last gardener we had was much more careful.

1068
59:14.698 --> 59:17.409
[Jae-hee] Check if he's sleeping, retrieve the spy cam glasses,

1069
59:17.534 --> 59:19.203
and then, the room.

1070
59:22.623 --> 59:23.624
[knocks on door]

1071
59:23.832 --> 59:24.917
I've got your drinks here, sir.

1072
59:27.669 --> 59:28.587
[latch clicks]

1073
59:30.089 --> 59:37.054
[tense percussive music playing]

1074
59:40.599 --> 59:41.600
[sighs]

1075
59:42.726 --> 59:43.852
[exhales sharply]

1076
59:52.569 --> 59:53.570
[sighs]

1077
59:58.909 --> 59:59.868
Mr. Yoon?

1078
01:00:02.037 --> 01:00:04.289
[Jae-hee] What the? Is he really asleep?

1079
01:00:06.500 --> 01:00:08.585
Mr. Yoon.

1080
01:00:11.839 --> 01:00:15.008
-[gasps] -[motor whirring]

1081
01:00:16.510 --> 01:00:17.594
Whoa.

1082
01:00:17.678 --> 01:00:19.138
[gentle resonant music playing]

1083
01:00:27.896 --> 01:00:29.106
[dramatic drum beats]

1084
01:00:34.486 --> 01:00:35.779
[door opening]

1085
01:00:40.075 --> 01:00:42.828
[tense atmospheric music playing]

1086
01:00:50.586 --> 01:00:51.712
[exhales]

1087
01:00:55.007 --> 01:00:56.008
[gasps]

1088
01:01:00.220 --> 01:01:03.223
[tense atmospheric music continues]

1089
01:01:05.350 --> 01:01:06.518
You.

1090
01:01:08.604 --> 01:01:09.646
[sighs]

1091
01:01:11.899 --> 01:01:13.525
Did I say you could enter?

1092
01:01:13.609 --> 01:01:17.654
Oh, I brought some drinks for you. Miss Choi prepared them.

1093
01:01:18.447 --> 01:01:20.157
I'll go downstairs and be on standby.

1094
01:01:21.992 --> 01:01:23.243
Yesterday…

1095
01:01:23.327 --> 01:01:25.162
[upbeat funky music playing]

1096
01:01:28.665 --> 01:01:30.209
[sighs]

1097
01:01:30.918 --> 01:01:33.045
I realized that I may have assumed…

1098
01:01:34.671 --> 01:01:36.965
Uh, sorry, what was that about yesterday, sir?

1099
01:01:39.426 --> 01:01:41.803
It seems I misinterpreted your intentions.

1100
01:01:41.887 --> 01:01:44.515
However, I believe anyone in my position would have thought as I did.

1101
01:01:46.099 --> 01:01:47.935
Yes, I'm listening. Please continue.

1102
01:01:48.143 --> 01:01:50.646
As I already told you, I never trust people, only situations,

1103
01:01:50.729 --> 01:01:53.565
and in this case, I was simply interpreting the situation we were in.

1104
01:01:53.732 --> 01:01:55.025
You follow?

1105
01:01:55.108 --> 01:01:56.568
Yes, I do, sure. Yes.

1106
01:01:56.652 --> 01:01:58.654
-I'll think this over outside. -[Yi-jun] Do it here.

1107
01:02:00.072 --> 01:02:02.366
For the first time in a while, I've made up my mind.

1108
01:02:03.200 --> 01:02:04.660
-Anyway… -[gasps]

1109
01:02:10.958 --> 01:02:14.711
[dramatic cheeky music playing]

1110
01:02:14.920 --> 01:02:15.921
What I wanna say is…

1111
01:02:17.506 --> 01:02:18.840
[groans]

1112
01:02:18.924 --> 01:02:20.342
Here's what I'm getting at.

1113
01:02:21.218 --> 01:02:23.178
-Can you please stop moving? -I'm just--

1114
01:02:23.262 --> 01:02:24.888
-[Jae-hee] I heard you. -Wait. Where do you think you're going?

1115
01:02:24.972 --> 01:02:26.390
-I'm talking to you. -I said I get it!

1116
01:02:26.473 --> 01:02:29.017
[Yi-jun yelps]

1117
01:02:29.101 --> 01:02:30.102
[groaning]

1118
01:02:31.812 --> 01:02:32.813
[gasps]

1119
01:02:33.772 --> 01:02:34.982
[gasps]

1120
01:02:35.065 --> 01:02:36.233
[grunts]

1121
01:02:36.316 --> 01:02:39.611
[dramatic music playing]

1122
01:02:40.821 --> 01:02:43.448
♪ Oh, not tonight ♪

1123
01:02:43.532 --> 01:02:47.327
♪ Oh, no, baby ♪

1124
01:02:47.411 --> 01:02:51.790
♪ I'm coming out ♪

1125
01:02:53.458 --> 01:02:57.462
♪ Through the fire and the rain ♪

1126
01:02:57.546 --> 01:02:58.714
[grunts]

1127
01:03:00.424 --> 01:03:04.845
♪ I won't let you go ♪

1128
01:03:04.928 --> 01:03:07.889
♪ Stay alive ♪

1129
01:03:10.976 --> 01:03:17.691
♪ Just hold on to me ♪

1130
01:03:17.774 --> 01:03:21.111
-[handcuffs clinking] -[paper tearing]

1131
01:03:21.820 --> 01:03:24.698
[gentle piano music playing]

1132
01:03:40.297 --> 01:03:44.926
♪ Say all the things you keep from me ♪

1133
01:03:45.802 --> 01:03:47.554
[Yi-jun] I get roped into one thing after another.

1134
01:03:48.096 --> 01:03:50.807
-I'm the one who did it to them. -Are you saying you did this, Mr. Yoon?

1135
01:03:50.891 --> 01:03:52.934
[Yi-jun] It seems you're the only one he hates.

1136
01:03:53.018 --> 01:03:55.562
Keep me safe until I fall asleep.

1137
01:03:55.646 --> 01:03:57.022
Let's have dinner together.

1138
01:03:57.105 --> 01:03:58.899
Ms. Lee, you're full of surprises, aren't you?

1139
01:03:58.982 --> 01:04:00.192
[tense dramatic music playing]

1140
01:04:00.275 --> 01:04:02.653
[Jae-hee] Something's happening in this house without my knowing.

1141
01:04:03.195 --> 01:04:04.863
[Na-jung] You know Yi-jun's new secretary?

1142
01:04:04.946 --> 01:04:06.281
He and I should meet up soon.

1143
01:04:06.365 --> 01:04:07.908
[Yi-jun] Weren't you just in this for the money?

1144
01:04:07.991 --> 01:04:08.909
I found it.

1145
01:04:08.992 --> 01:04:10.118
Turn around immediately.

1146
01:04:10.202 --> 01:04:11.745
You're fired, effective immediately.

1147
01:04:12.037 --> 01:04:13.497
Get out of my house, now!

1148
01:04:13.580 --> 01:04:15.290
[gentle closing music playing]
